.TH CUPSFILTER 8 "2026-11-18" "Presswork 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
cupsfilter \- Presswork standalone CUPS MIME and PPD filter-chain converter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cupsfilter
.RB [ \-\-list\-filters ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR cupsd.conf ]
.RB [ \-d
.IR printer ]
.RB [ \-D ]
.RB [ \-e ]
.RB [ \-i
.IR mime/type ]
.RB [ \-j
.IR job\-id [, N ]]
.RB [ \-m
.IR mime/type ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR copies ]
.RB [ \-o
.IR name=value ]
.RB [ \-p
.IR filename.ppd ]
.RB [ \-P
.IR filename.ppd ]
.RB [ \-t
.IR title ]
.RB [ \-u ]
.RB [ \-U
.IR username ]
.RI [ filename ]
.br
.B cupsfilter
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.br
.B cupsfilter
.RB [ \-V | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cupsfilter
converts a document from one MIME media type to another using the same MIME
database
.RI ( mime.types ", " mime.convs ", " local.types ", " local.convs ),
PPD
.B *cupsFilter
/
.B *cupsFilter2
rules, and least-cost Dijkstra filter graph used by Presswork
.BR cupsd (8).
Converted output is written to standard output, while filter diagnostics appear
on standard error.
.PP
When
.I filename
is omitted or given as
.BR \- ,
.B cupsfilter
streams standard input to a secure temporary spool file (mode
.BR 0600 ,
automatically cleaned up on exit) so MIME auto-detection and multi-stage filter
chains work identically to file inputs.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-list\-filters
Print the resolved filter chain (one filter per line) to standard output and
exit without executing any filter.
Strictly read-only: preserves input and PPD files even if
.B \-D
or
.B \-u
was also supplied.
.TP
.BI \-c " cupsd.conf"
Load configuration from an alternate
.I cupsd.conf
(and its sibling
.IR cups\-files.conf )
to resolve
.BR DataDir ,
.BR ServerRoot ,
.BR ServerBin ,
and
.BR RequestRoot .
.TP
.BI \-d " printer"
Use the named printer queue (resolving its PPD from
.I ServerRoot/ppd/<printer>.ppd
when
.B \-p
is not specified).
.TP
.B \-D
Delete the input file after a successful conversion (ignored under
.BR \-\-list\-filters ).
.TP
.B \-e
Use every matching filter declared in the PPD file.
.TP
.BI \-i " mime/type"
Override input MIME media type instead of auto-detecting via
.IR mime.types .
.TP
.BI \-j " job\-id" \fR[\fP, N \fR]\fP
Convert document
.I N
(default:
.BR 1 )
of spooled job
.I job\-id
from
.IR RequestRoot .
.TP
.BI \-m " mime/type"
Set the target output MIME media type (default:
.BR application/pdf ).
Use
.B printer/foo
or a concrete type such as
.BR image/pwg\-raster ,
.BR application/vnd.cups\-raster ,
or
.BR application/postscript .
.TP
.BI \-n " copies"
Set the copy count passed to filters as
.B argv[4]
(positive integer; default:
.BR 1 ).
.TP
.BI \-o " name=value"
Pass a job option to the filter chain in
.B argv[5]
(bare names such as
.B \-o landscape
expand to
.BR landscape=true ).
May be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-p " filename.ppd" "\fR, \fP\-P " filename.ppd
Specify the PPD file to use for
.B *cupsFilter
/
.B *cupsFilter2
resolution and the
.B PPD
environment variable.
.B \-P
is an alias for
.BR \-p .
.TP
.BI \-t " title"
Set the job title passed as
.B argv[3]
(defaults to the input filename).
.TP
.B \-u
Delete the PPD file after a successful conversion (ignored under
.BR \-\-list\-filters ).
.TP
.BI \-U " username"
Set the username passed as
.B argv[2]
(defaults to the current user).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage summary and exit with status 0.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show Presswork version information and exit with status 0.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CUPS_SERVERROOT
Override configuration directory (default:
.IR /etc/cups ).
.TP
.B CUPS_DATADIR
Override shared data / MIME directory (default:
.IR /usr/share/cups ).
.TP
.B CUPS_SERVERBIN
Override filter binary directory (default:
.IR /usr/lib/cups ).
.TP
.B CUPS_REQUESTROOT
Override spool directory used by
.B \-j
(default:
.IR /var/spool/cups ).
.TP
.B TMPDIR
Directory used for temporary stdin spool files.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Conversion or
.B \-\-list\-filters
succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, missing file/PPD, no valid conversion chain found in the
MIME database, or a filter stage exited with a non-zero status.
.SH EXAMPLES
Inspect which filters would run to convert a text file to PDF:
.PP
.EX
cupsfilter \-\-list\-filters \-m application/pdf /etc/hostname
.EE
.PP
Convert a PostScript document to PDF using a specific printer's PPD:
.PP
.EX
cupsfilter \-p /etc/cups/ppd/office.ppd \-m application/pdf input.ps > output.pdf
.EE
.PP
Test filter chain resolution against a shadow configuration:
.PP
.EX
cupsfilter \-\-list\-filters \-c /tmp/pw\-shadow/etc/cupsd.conf \-d office \-m image/pwg\-raster doc.pdf
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/bin/cupsfilter
Filter-chain utility.
.TP
.I /usr/share/cups/mime/mime.types
.TQ
.I /usr/share/cups/mime/mime.convs
Standard MIME type and conversion rules.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/cups/filter/
Installed filter executables (supplied by
.B cups\-filters
or printer drivers).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cupsd (8),
.BR cupsd.conf (5),
.BR cups\-files.conf (5),
.BR lp (1)
